Payment workflow:

Customer selects a package.

Backend obtains the authoritative package price and tenant.

Backend creates a pending payment record with a unique transaction reference.

Backend initiates the supported M-Pesa payment request.

Customer receives the payment prompt.

Safaricom calls the configured HTTPS callback.

Backend validates the callback against the transaction and expected amount, tenant, reference and available provider identifiers.

Backend marks the payment successful, failed or pending.

Duplicate callbacks are processed idempotently.

Only confirmed successful payments activate packages.

Customer and router owner see the updated transaction.

The system issues a receipt.

